    "layout": "cover",
    "content": "> A single-file static documentation engine with RTL support, themes, instant search, and one-click export to plain markdown.\n\nLumen packs an entire documentation system into a single HTML file. No build step. No server. No framework. Open it in any modern browser and start writing.\n\n[badge:success:Single File] [badge:info:Zero Build] [badge:warning:RTL-Aware] [badge:neutral:~80KB]\n\n## What you are looking at\n\nThis page — the sidebar, the search box, the themes, the command palette, the markdown you are reading right now — is rendered by an engine written in vanilla JavaScript and embedded inside one HTML file.\n\nThe engine reads pages from an in-memory array, renders them with `marked.js` + `highlight.js` + `KaTeX` + `Mermaid`, and lets you export them as individual `.md` files plus an `assets/` folder for embedded images.\n\n## Start exploring\n\n- Use the **sidebar** on the left to navigate.\n- Press [kbd:⌘K] to open the **command palette**.\n- Press [kbd:G] for the **outline grid view**.\n- Press [kbd:T] to cycle **themes**.\n- Press [kbd:?] any time — it reopens this palette.\n\n:::tip\nEverything you do here — pages you write, bookmarks, last-visited history — is saved to your browser's `localStorage`. Clearing your browser data resets Lumen to this default documentation.\n:::\n\n## A guided tour in three arcs\n\n:::card-grid\n:::card Theory\nWhy single-file? Why simplification? What does RTL really mean? Three essays on the ideas behind Lumen.\n:::\n:::card Practice\nMarkdown reference, custom extensions, themes, keyboard shortcuts, search, export. Everything you need to use Lumen.\n:::\n:::card Vision\nA manifesto on documentation as a craft, plus the roadmap of features I would build next.\n:::\n:::\n\nChoose your arc, or just press [kbd:⌘K] and jump anywhere.\n"
