    "dir": "ltr",
    "content": "# Welcome to Lumen\n\nLumen is built on a simple thesis: documentation should travel as easily as a single file, run anywhere a browser runs, and feel as polished as a hosted product.\n\n## What is inside\n\n- **A markdown engine** with code highlighting, math (KaTeX), and Mermaid diagrams\n- **Custom extensions**: callouts, cards, badges, key bindings, collapsible details\n- **Full RTL support** — switch the entire UI to Persian or Arabic with one click\n- **Five themes**: Midnight, Glass, Daylight, Sepia, Terminal\n- **Instant search & command palette** for navigation by muscle memory\n- **An in-place editor** to write and edit pages directly inside the document\n- **Export to .md + assets** — generate a downloadable zip with one click\n- **Bookmarks, history, reading progress** — all stored locally, all private\n\n## What Lumen is not\n\n- It is **not** a wiki. There is no multi-user editing, no revision history beyond your browser.\n- It is **not** a publishing platform. There is no hosting, no RSS, no analytics.\n- It is **not** a static site generator. There is no build pipeline.\n\nLumen is a **single-document workshop**. You write, you read, you export. If you need a wiki, use one. If you need a publishing platform, use one. If you need to ship a beautiful, self-contained piece of documentation in one file, use Lumen.\n\n## How to use it\n\n1. **Browse** the default documentation using the sidebar or keyboard.\n2. **Edit any page** by pressing [kbd:E] — the editor opens with the current page.\n3. **Create new pages** with the same editor; they appear in the sidebar under \"Custom\".\n4. **Export** with the download icon in the top bar. You get a zip of `.md` files.\n5. **Import** by dragging `.md` files onto the window, or via the settings panel.\n\n:::info\nThe demo content you are reading right now is itself just an array of page objects. Open the editor on this page to see the raw markdown.\n:::\n\n## A note on performance\n\nLumen is built to feel instant. Search is indexed at startup. Routing is hash-based — no network round-trips. Rendering happens in a single pass per page. The whole engine fits in about 1,500 lines of JavaScript and weighs roughly 80 kilobytes before the CDN libraries load.\n\nThe Performance page breaks down the techniques used to keep it that way.\n"
